            <ArticleTitle>Gadolinium enhancement of spinal subdural collection on magnetic resonance imaging after lumbar puncture.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>553-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 35-year-old male with an unusual contrast-enhancing sterile spinal subdural collection on magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), apparently occurring as a complication of lumbar puncture. Follow-up MRI after 4 weeks demonstrated spontaneous resolution of the collection without intervening treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
